G-C2.2: interruptions and incidents. Written by the operator; times are UTC, which is the laptop's local time.

1. Pause and restart of the laptop during the run of seed 5 (13 to 14 November 2026)

Before
- 13 November 21:13: the owner wrote that he would pause the run, close the runner's window, restart the laptop to
  install Windows updates, use the GPU for other things, and then continue the run. The runbook allows a pause of a training
  run and says that after a restart the queue is started again.
- The host as recorded before: Windows-11-10.0.26200-SP0 (gate_records/smoke/smoke_report.json, 13 November 12:46 to
  12:51); NVIDIA driver 610.74 (logs/setup_log.txt, 10 November); Python 3.12.16, numpy 2.4.6, scipy 1.18.1,
  torch 2.12.1+cu132.

What happened
- 21:17:53: the checkpoint of epoch 75 was written (gate_runs/label_free_s5/state.pt).
- 21:19:05: the owner paused the run (tools/pause.py; the record is queue/PAUSED_20261114_014256.json).
  21:19:08: the runner stopped the job 74_c22_train_s5 (its done file: returncode 1, killed true). The 75 s of work on
  epoch 76 were lost. The waiting job 74_c22_train_s5_b_hold started.
- 21:20:15: the owner closed the runner's window. The waiting job ended with code 3221225786. The runner was stopped
  while it wrote that job's done file: an empty queue/74_c22_train_s5_b_hold.done.json.tmp was left and no done file,
  so the waiting job stayed pending. No guard ran and no later job was cancelled.
- For the time between 21:20 and 01:40 the owner had announced a restart of the laptop. Whether it took place and
  which updates were installed is not known to the operator at the time of writing; it is added below when known.
- 14 November 01:40 to 01:42: the operator checked the files before the run went on: the queue as described;
  state.pt of 82,366,333 bytes, a zip archive of 455 entries without a CRC error; attempts.log with its one start line.
- 01:42:56: the owner continued the run (tools/resume.py: queue/74_c22_train_s5_c.job.json with the same command).
  01:43:07: he started the runner again (start.bat). The waiting job ran again and ended at once with code 0, and
  74_c22_train_s5_c started.
- gate_runs/label_free_s5/attempts.log: "2026-11-14T01:43:10+00:00 start", "2026-11-14T01:44:51+00:00 resumed from
  epoch 75".
- 01:48:03: epoch 76 ended with loss 10.4179 in 191.64 s (epochs 73 to 75 before the pause: 10.4481, 10.4185, 10.3804
  in 350.03, 368.22 and 360.81 s).

Effect
- No training between 21:19:08 and 01:44:51 (4 h 26 min). The run is the same run, resumed from its checkpoint, as
  the pre-specification provides.
- The software of the host may have changed during the run of seed 5 (Windows updates). No threshold, metric,
  reading or seed changed.

Note on the queue (a script outside the stamp)
- When the runner's window is closed, the running job can end a moment before the runner does. Here the runner had
  begun to record the waiting job as ended. Had it finished, the next start of the runner would have gone to the
  guard 74z_c22_guard before the continuation existed, and the guard would have cancelled the later jobs. This did
  not happen. After a closed window the continuation is therefore queued first (tools/resume.py) and the runner is
  started second, the order used here.
